14
01:32:36,923 --> 01:32:42,923
Cloud Atlas is a 2012 epic science fiction film written and
directed by the Wachowskis and Tom Tykwer.

15
01:39:13,846 --> 01:39:19,846
Based on the 2004 novel by David Mitchell, it has multiple plots occurring during six eras and
features an ensemble cast who perform multiple roles across these time periods.

16
01:45:50,769 --> 01:45:56,769
The film was produced by Grant Hill and Stefan Arndt, in
addition to the Wachowskis and Tykwer.

17
01:52:27,692 --> 01:52:33,692
During its four years of development, the producers had
difficulties securing financial support.

18
01:59:04,615 --> 01:59:10,615
It was eventually produced with a budget between US$100 million and US$146.7 million provided by
independent sources, making it one of the most expensive independent films ever produced.

19
02:05:41,538 --> 02:05:47,538
Filming for Cloud Atlas began in September 2011 at
Babelsberg Studio in Potsdam-Babelsberg, Germany.

20
02:12:18,461 --> 02:12:24,461
It premiered on 8 September 2012 at the 37th Toronto International Film Festival, and was
publicly released on 26 October 2012 in conventional and IMAX cinemas.

21
02:18:55,384 --> 02:19:01,384
Critics were polarized, causing it to be included on
various "Best Film" and "Worst Film" lists.

22
02:25:32,307 --> 02:25:38,307
It was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Original Score for Tykwer
(who co-scored the film), Johnny Klimek, and Reinhold Heil.

23
02:32:09,230 --> 02:32:15,230
It received several nominations at the Saturn Awards, including Best
Science Fiction Film, and won for Best Editing and Best Make-up.

24
02:38:46,153 --> 02:38:52,153
The film explores themes of future, artificial intelligence (a.i.),
based on novel or book, san francisco, california, clone.

25
02:45:23,076 --> 02:45:29,076
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
